<h3 id="one-page-training-recipe-tear-out-and-keep">One-page training recipe (tear out and keep)</h3>
<p><strong>Setup.</strong> Backbone: ResNet-50 (default) or EfficientNet-B0 (limited compute); weights: torchvision IMAGENET1K_V2 / timm pretrained — record exact version. Input: resize per backbone (224 / 380), normalize with ImageNet mean/std when using ImageNet weights. Split by the right unit (patient / site / region), stratified, seed fixed.</p>
<p><strong>Augmentation.</strong> Train: RandomResizedCrop + horizontal flip (p=0.5, unless domain forbids) + mild color/intensity jitter + one advanced method (RandAugment or CutMix). Validate: deterministic resize + center crop. Inspect 64 augmented samples before training.</p>
<p><strong>Optimization.</strong> AdamW, lr 3e-4 (from scratch) / 1e-4 backbone + 1e-3 head (fine-tune); weight decay 0.05 / 0.01; cosine schedule with 5–10% warmup; mixed precision on; label smoothing 0.1; early stopping patience 10–20 on validation loss.</p>
<p><strong>Protocol.</strong> Stage 1: train head only (5–10 epochs). Stage 2: unfreeze, discriminative LRs, 20–50 epochs. 3+ seeds, mean ± std. Ablate: pretraining, augmentation, backbone — one row per decision.</p>
<p><strong>Evaluation.</strong> Metrics for the domain (F1/AUC/Dice, not just accuracy); confusion matrix; Grad-CAM on 20+ samples incl. failures; bootstrap CI for close comparisons; report params, FLOPs, and measured latency.</p>
<p><strong>Before submitting.</strong> Paper ledger complete; dataset versioned; code + weights + figure scripts released; limitations paragraph written; every number in the paper traced to a log line.</p>
<h2 id="appendix-a-complete-training-loop-template">Appendix A — Complete Training Loop Template</h2>
<p>The following is a minimal but complete training script incorporating this book's recommendations. Adapt it; don't rewrite from memory each time.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">import torch, torch.nn as nn
from torch.utils.data import DataLoader
from torch.amp import GradScaler, autocast
from torchvision import models, transforms

# ---------- config (log all of these) ----------
NUM_CLASSES, EPOCHS, BATCH, SEED = 10, 50, 32, 0
torch.manual_seed(SEED)

train_tf = transforms.Compose([
    transforms.RandomResizedCrop(224, scale=(0.5, 1.0)),
    transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(),
    transforms.ColorJitter(0.2, 0.2, 0.2, 0.05),
    transforms.ToTensor(),
    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),
])
val_tf = transforms.Compose([
    transforms.Resize(256), transforms.CenterCrop(224), transforms.ToTensor(),
    transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225]),
])
# train_ds / val_ds built with the right split unit (patient/site/region)

# ---------- model ----------
model = models.resnet50(weights=models.ResNet50_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V2)
model.fc = nn.Linear(model.fc.in_features, NUM_CLASSES)
model.cuda()

# Stage 1: head only
for p in model.parameters(): p.requires_grad = False
for p in model.fc.parameters(): p.requires_grad = True
opt = torch.optim.AdamW(model.fc.parameters(), lr=1e-3, weight_decay=0.01)

def run_epoch(loader, train):
    model.train(train)
    tot_loss, correct, n = 0.0, 0, 0
    for x, y in loader:
        x, y = x.cuda(), y.cuda()
        with autocast(device_type='cuda'), torch.set_grad_enabled(train):
            out = model(x)
            loss = nn.CrossEntropyLoss(label_smoothing=0.1)(out, y)
        if train:
            opt.zero_grad(); scaler.scale(loss).backward()
            scaler.step(opt); scaler.update()
        tot_loss += loss.item() * len(x); correct += (out.argmax(1) == y).sum().item(); n += len(x)
    return tot_loss / n, correct / n

scaler = GradScaler()
train_loader = DataLoader(train_ds, batch_size=BATCH, shuffle=True, num_workers=4)
val_loader = DataLoader(val_ds, batch_size=BATCH, num_workers=4)
for ep in range(5):
    tr_loss, tr_acc = run_epoch(train_loader, True)
    va_loss, va_acc = run_epoch(val_loader, False)
    print(f&quot;[head] ep{ep} train {tr_loss:.3f}/{tr_acc:.3f} val {va_loss:.3f}/{va_acc:.3f}&quot;)

# Stage 2: fine-tune all with discriminative LRs
for p in model.parameters(): p.requires_grad = True
opt = torch.optim.AdamW([
    {'params': model.layer4.parameters(), 'lr': 1e-4},
    {'params': model.fc.parameters(), 'lr': 1e-3},
], lr=1e-5, weight_decay=0.01)
sched = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(opt, T_max=EPOCHS)

best, patience, wait = float('inf'), 10, 0
for ep in range(EPOCHS):
    tr_loss, tr_acc = run_epoch(train_loader, True)
    va_loss, va_acc = run_epoch(val_loader, False)
    sched.step()
    print(f&quot;ep{ep} train {tr_loss:.3f}/{tr_acc:.3f} val {va_loss:.3f}/{va_acc:.3f}&quot;)
    if va_loss &lt; best:
        best, wait = va_loss, 0
        torch.save({'model': model.state_dict(), 'epoch': ep}, 'best.pt')
    else:
        wait += 1
        if wait &gt;= patience:
            print(&quot;early stopping&quot;); break
</code></pre>
<p>Deliberate choices encoded above: staged fine-tuning, discriminative LRs, AMP, label smoothing, cosine schedule, early stopping on validation loss with best-checkpoint saving. The main things it omits (add as needed): weighted sampling for imbalance, gradient accumulation for small GPUs, LR warmup (add a linear warmup scheduler for the first epochs), and multi-seed looping (wrap in a <code>for seed in [0,1,2]</code> shell loop).</p>
<h2 id="appendix-b-notation-and-shape-conventions">Appendix B — Notation and Shape Conventions</h2>
<ul>
<li>Tensors: <strong>NCHW</strong> — (batch, channels, height, width). A "224px RGB batch of 32" is (32, 3, 224, 224).</li>
<li>Conv2d weight shape: (C_out, C_in, K_h, K_w). The i-th output channel's kernel is <code>weight[i]</code>.</li>
<li>"3×3 conv, 64→128" means kernel 3×3, 64 input channels, 128 output channels: params = 128 × (9×64 + 1).</li>
<li>RF: receptive field; s: stride; P: padding. Output size: floor((W − K + 2P)/S) + 1.</li>
<li>lr: learning rate; wd: weight decay; TTA: test-time augmentation; GAP: global average pooling.</li>
<li>"Frozen" = <code>requires_grad=False</code>; "eval mode" = <code>model.eval()</code> (affects BN/dropout, independent of freezing).</li>
<li>Seeds: report data seed and init seed separately when diagnosing variance.</li>
</ul>
